WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.400
An agent is a program that reads a request,
picks its own tools, and uses them.

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.248
Our campaign pipelines were separate jobs,

3
00:00:09.248 --> 00:00:12.396
and someone had to start each
with the right settings.

4
00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:16.213
I designed and built one agent
to sit in front of them all.

5
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:19.590
You send it one plain-English
sentence, like:

6
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.594
schedule a marketing
campaign for the next day.

7
00:00:22.894 --> 00:00:25.793
The agent sets that sentence
beside its four tools.

8
00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:31.136
Create a campaign, scrape product data,
search web trends, check a running job.

9
00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:37.135
A language model running on Cloudflare reads
both, and answers with a plan in JSON.

10
00:00:37.385 --> 00:00:41.182
Each action names a tool, its
settings, and the reason for it.

11
00:00:41.482 --> 00:00:45.844
The agent pulls the plan out of the
reply and checks each tool name.

12
00:00:46.094 --> 00:00:49.251
Then it starts each job
as a Cloudflare Workflow,

13
00:00:49.251 --> 00:00:51.700
which saves its progress step by step.

14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.267
It sends back its decision trail, so
you can see what it chose and why.

15
00:00:56.767 --> 00:01:02.764
I also published it as an MCP server, the
standard way AI tools call each other.

16
00:01:03.014 --> 00:01:09.248
Other agents and Claude clients
reach it over SSE, HTTP, or RPC.

17
00:01:09.648 --> 00:01:12.299
The new scheduler hands
its jobs to it too.
